                    \&amp;\stackrel{\frac{1}{2}\hat \mathbf{p}_1}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{H}_{diff}(X,\mathbf{B}^3 U(1))
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the right vertical morphism is a choice of (any) one point in each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
              (differential cohomology class) of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 3
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{diff}(X,\mathbf{B}^3 U(1))
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
              is independent of this choice).
            %p
              More specifically, a
              %strong geometric string structure
              is a twisted differential string structure whose differential twist has underlying trivial class.
          .num_note
            %h6#note Note
            %p
              In terms of local
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+valued+differential+forms"} ∞-Lie algebra valued differential forms
              data this has been considered in (
              %a{:href => "#SSSIII"}> SSSIII
              ), as we shall discuss
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#ChernWeilTheory"} below
            %p
              For the case where the the underlying integral class of the twist is trivial – geometric string structures – something close to this definition, explicitly modeled on
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+2-gerbe"} bundle 2-gerbe
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Waldorf"} Waldorf
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Properties"} below
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#GeneralProperties General
          #GroupoidOfStringStructures.num_prop
            %h6#observation Observation
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi String
                      %mrow
                        %mi tw
                        %mo ,
                        %mi diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} String_{tw,diff}(X)
              of twisted differential string structures is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-truncated"} 2-truncated
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This follows from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
              associated to the defining
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mi diff
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mn 3
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{diff}(X, \mathbf{B}^3 U(1))
                  is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-groupoid"} 3-groupoid
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi Spin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}(X, \mathbf{B}Spin)
                  is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-groupoid"} 1-groupoid
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi H
                          %mi diff
                          %mn 4
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^4_{diff}(X)
                  is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-groupoid"} 0-groupoid
          %p
            See also (
            %a{:href => "#Waldorf"}> Waldorf, cor. 1.1.5
            ).
          #PropertiesOfTrivialIntegralTwistClass.num_prop
            %h6#observation_2 Observation
            %p
              If the underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
              class of the twist is trivial,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi tw
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c(tw) = 0 \in H^3(X, \mathbb{Z})
              = succeed "-twisted" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi tw
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tw
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
              are characterized by a globally defined 3-form on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This 3-form is the globally defined connection 3-form of an appropriate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 3-bundle with connection
            equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CS(\nabla)
            whose underlying 3-bundle is by assumption trivial: on a trivial circle
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-form." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            This statement appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Waldorf"}> Waldorf, theorem 1.3.3
            ), where circle 3-bundles are modeled as
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+2-gerbe"} bundle 2-gerbe
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Elements in the defining
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialStringStructure"}
              over a given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi Spin
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi conn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla \in \mathbf{H}(X,\mathbf{B} Spin)_{conn}
              are chracterized by an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi diff
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\alpha] \in H^4_{diff}(X)
              and an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo :
                    %mi CS
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∇
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega : CS(\nabla) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \alpha
            %p
              between the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle
              and the given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 3-bundle
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi CS
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ∇
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c(CS(\nabla)) = c(\alpha) = 0
            %p
              By the
              %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/ordinary%20differential%20cohomology#AbstractProperties"} characteristic class exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi int
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi diff
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to \Omega^3(X)/\Omega_{int}^{3}(X)
                    \\to
                    H^4_{diff}(X) \stackrel{c}{\to} H^4(X, \mathbb{Z})
            %p
              any two classes in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 3
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi diff
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 \mathbf{H}_{diff}(X, \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)) \simeq H^4_{diff}(X)
              that have trivial underlying class in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 3
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 \mathbf{H}(X, \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)) \simeq H^4(X, \mathbb{Z})
              differ by a 3-form modulo a closed 3-form with integral periods.
            %p
              Therefore both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\alpha]
              as well as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi CS
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∇
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi diff
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CS(\nabla)] \in H^4_{diff}(X)
              are given by a globally defined 3-form modulo an integral form: the global connection 3-form on these trivial
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 3-bundles with connection
          %h3#ChernWeilTheory
            Construction in terms of
            = succeed "-Cech" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            We use the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            (as described there) by the local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msubsup
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mi smooth
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi sSet
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mi proj
                      %mo ,
                      %mi loc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp_{smooth}^{op}, sSet]_{proj,loc}
            to give an explicit construction of twisted differential string structures in terms of
            = succeed "-cocycles" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+valued+differential+forms"} ∞-Lie algebra valued differential forms
          %p
            Proofs not displayed here can be found at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+string+structure+--+proofs"} differential string structure – proofs
            \.
          %p
            Recall the following fact from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+theory+in+Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Chern-Weil theory in Smooth∞Grpd
            (
            %a{:href => "#FSS"}> FSS
            ).
          #LieIntegrationOfDifferentialPOne.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The differential fractional Pontryagin class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{2} \hat \mathbf{p}_1
              is presented in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi smooth
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp_{smooth}^{op}, sSet]_{proj}
              by the top morphism of simplicial presheaves in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi cosk
                              %mn 3
                            %mi exp
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔰𝔬
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mi ChW
                                %mo ,
                                %mi smp
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi exp
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi μ
                                %mo ,
                                %mi cs
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 3
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mrow
                                %mi ChW
                                %mo ,
                                %mi smp
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi cosk
                              %mn 3
                            %mi exp
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔰𝔬
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mi diff
                                %mo ,
                                %mi smp
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi exp
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi μ
                                %mo ,
                                %mi cs
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 3
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mi smp
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %msub
                              %mi Spin
                              %mi c
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{cosk}_3\exp(\mathfrak{so})_{ChW,smp}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\exp(\mu, cs)}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^3 \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}_{ChW,smp}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{cosk}_3\exp(\mathfrak{so})_{diff,smp}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\exp(\mu, cs)}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^3 \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}_{smp}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{B}Spin_{c}
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            Here the middle morphism is the direct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} L-∞ algebra cocycle
            while the top morphisms is its restriction to coefficients for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} ∞-connections
          %p
            In order to compute the
            = succeed "s" do
