            satisfied by these.
          %h3#differential_string_structures_and_fermionic_string_quantum_anomalies Differential string structures and fermionic string quantum anomalies
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pfaffian+line+bundle"} Pfaffian line bundle
            controlling the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermionic+path+integral"} fermionic path integral
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+superstring"} heterotic superstring
            propagating on target
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            trivializes precisely if the target has a (geometric) string structure.
          %p
            One shows that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pfaffian+line+bundle"} Pfaffian line bundle
            on the worldsheet is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphic"} isomorphic
            as a bundle with connection with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            of the differential string structure on the target space to the mapping space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,X]
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly"} quantum anomaly
          %p
            (First argued in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Killingback"} Killingback
            = succeed "))." do
              %a{:href => "#Bunke"} Bunke
          %h3#InheteroticSugra The Green-Schwarz mechanism in heterotic supergravity
          %p
            We discuss the application of twisted differential string structures in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %p
            Local differential form data as in note
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnwindingTheLocalData"}
            above is known in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory+and+physics"} theoretical physics
            in the context of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz mechanism
            for 10-dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
          %p In this context
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                is called the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+connection"} spin connection
            %li
              %p
                the components
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 3
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((H_3)_i, \cdots)
                of the above cocycle are known as the
                = succeed "-twisted" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi 𝒢
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \mathcal{G}_4
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kalb-Ramond+field"} Kalb-Ramond field
          %p
            In this application the twisting cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi diff
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \mathcal{G}_4 \in H^4_{diff}(X)
            is itself the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle
            of a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            with local connection form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔲
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \Omega^1(U, \mathfrak{u})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_3 = CS(A)
            and the above local form data becomes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %mi d
                  %mi B
                  %mo +
                  %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
